.\" Automatically generated by Pandoc 1.18
.\"
.TH "explain" "1" "" "SequoiaDB User Manuals" ""
.hy
.SH NAME
.PP
explain \- get the access plan for the query
.SH SYNOPSIS
.PP
\f[B]query.explain([options])\f[]
.SH CATEGORY
.PP
SdbQuery
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
This function is used to get the access plan for the query.
.SH PARAMETERS
.PP
options ( \f[I]object, optional\f[] )
.PP
The output information of the access plan can be controlled through the
parameter "options":
.IP \[bu] 2
Run ( \f[I]boolean\f[] ): Whether to run the access plan, and the default value
is "false".
.RS 2
.PP
The values are as follows:
.IP \[bu] 2
true: Run access plan and output access plan information.
.IP \[bu] 2
false: Only output access plan information, do not run.
.PP
Format: \f[C]Run: true\f[]
.RE
.IP \[bu] 2
Detail ( \f[I]boolean\f[] ): Whether to output detailed access plan, and the
default value is "false".
.RS 2
.PP
When the value of parameter "Detail" is "true", a layer of detailed access plan
is displayed by default.
.PP
The values are as follows:
.IP \[bu] 2
true: Displayed detailed access plan.
.IP \[bu] 2
false: Displayed normal access plan.
.PP
Format: \f[C]Detail: true\f[]
.RE
.IP \[bu] 2
Estimate ( \f[I]boolean\f[] ): Whether to display the estimate part of the
detailed access plan, and the default value is the value of the parameter
"Detail".
.RS 2
.PP
If parameter "Estimate" is explicitly set, parameter "Detail" will be
automatically set to "true".
.PP
The values are as follows:
.IP \[bu] 2
true: Display the estimated part.
.IP \[bu] 2
false：Do not display the estimated part.
.PP
Format: \f[C]Estimate: true\f[]
.RE
.IP \[bu] 2
Expand ( \f[I]boolean\f[] ): Whether to display the expanded information of the
detailed access plan, and the default value is "false", which means not to
display.
.RS 2
.PP
If parameter "Expand" is explicitly set, parameter "Detail" will be
automatically set to "true".
.PP
Format: \f[C]Expand: true\f[]
.RE
.IP \[bu] 2
Flatten ( \f[I]boolean\f[] ): Whether to display the access plan of each node
and each sub\-collection separately, and the default value is "false".
.RS 2
.PP
If parameter "Flatten" is explicitly set, parameter "Detail" and "Expand" will
be automatically set to "true".
.PP
The values are as follows:
.IP \[bu] 2
true: Display the access plan of each node and each sub\-collection separately.
.IP \[bu] 2
false: Combine the access plans of nodes and sub\-collections into an array and
hang them on the upper\-level node or main collection for display.
.PP
Format: \f[C]Flatten: true\f[]
.RE
.IP \[bu] 2
Filter ( \f[I]string/array\f[] ): Filter the details of the estimated results,
and the default value is "ALL".
.RS 2
.PP
If parameter "Filter" is explicitly set, parameter "Detail" and "Estimate" will
be automatically set to "true".
.PP
The values are as follows:
.IP \[bu] 2
"None": Do not display any details of the estimated results.
.IP \[bu] 2
"Input": Display input details of the estimated results.
.IP \[bu] 2
"Filter": Display filtering details of the estimated results.
.IP \[bu] 2
"Output": Display output details of the estimated results.
.IP \[bu] 2
"All": Display all details of the estimated results.
.PP
Format: \f[C]Filter: ["Input", "Output"]\f[]
.RE
.IP \[bu] 2
CMDLocation ( "object" ): Filter the results of the access plan according to the
data groups, and the default is null, which means that no filter condition is
set.
.RS 2
.IP \[bu] 2
Parameter "CMDLocation" only supports filtering by replication group ID
(corresponding to parameter "GroupID") and replication group name (corresponding
to parameter "GroupName").
.IP \[bu] 2
If parameter "CMDLocation" is explicitly set, parameter "Detail" will be
automatically set to "true".
.PP
Format: \f[C]CMDLocation: {GroupName: "group1"}\f[]
.RE
.IP \[bu] 2
SubCollections ( \f[I]string/array\f[] ): Filter the results of the access plan
according to one or multiple sub\-collections, and the default is null, which
means that no filter condition is set.
.RS 2
.IP \[bu] 2
This parameter only takes effect in the access plan involving the main
collection and sub\-collection.
.IP \[bu] 2
When specifying this parameter, it is necessary to specify the parameter
"Expand" as "true" at the same time.
.PP
Format: \f[C]SubCollections: ["subcs.subcl1", "subcs.subcl2"]\f[]
.RE
.IP \[bu] 2
Search ( \f[I]boolean\f[] ): Whether to display the search process of the access
plan, and the default value is "false", which means not to display.
.RS 2
.PP
If parameter "Search" is explicitly set, parameter "Detail" and "Expand" will be
automatically set to "true".
.PP
Format: \f[C]Search: true\f[]
.RE
.IP \[bu] 2
Evaluate ( \f[I]boolean\f[] ): Whether to display the deduction formula of the
query optimizer, and the default value is "false", which means not to display.
.RS 2
.PP
If parameter "Evaluate" is explicitly set, parameter "Detail", "Search" and
"Expand" will be automatically set to "true".
.PP
Format: \f[C]Evaluate: true\f[]
.RE
.IP \[bu] 2
Abbrev ( \f[I]boolean\f[] ): Whether to output long strings in abbreviation
mode, and the default value is "false", which means not to abbreviate the
output.
.RS 2
.PP
Format: \f[C]Abbrev: true\f[]
.RE
.SH RETURN VALUE
.PP
When the function executes successfully, it will return an object of type
SdbCursor.
Users can get the access plan of the query through this object, refer to access
plan.
.PP
When the function fails, an exception will be thrown and an error message will
be printed.
.SH ERRORS
.PP
When the exception happens, use getLastErrMsg() to get the error message or use
getLastError() to get the error code.
For more details, refer to Troubleshooting.
.SH VERSION
.PP
v2.0 and above
.SH EXAMPLES
.IP \[bu] 2
Get the normal access plan for a query.
.RS 2
.IP
.nf
\f[C]
> db.sample.employee.find({a:{$gte:100}}).explain()
{
  "NodeName": "hostname:11820",
  "GroupName": "group1",
  "Role": "data",
  "Name": "sample.employee",
  "ScanType": "tbscan",
  "IndexName": "",
  "UseExtSort": false,
  "Query": {
    "$and": [
      {
        "a": {
          "$gte": 100
        }
      }
    ]
  },
  "IXBound": null,
  "NeedMatch": true,
  "IndexCover": false,
  "ReturnNum": 49892,
  "ElapsedTime": 0.323423,
  "IndexRead": 0,
  "DataRead": 49945,
  "UserCPU": 0.1399999999999999,
  "SysCPU": 0
}
\&...
